      "item": "theoreticalsciences:markov_chain_refinery",
      "title": "Markov Chain Refinery",
      "text": "Three vats in a ring, the feed hopping between them by tuned chances. Where it spends its time - the chain's steady state - decides what it becomes.$(br2)$(thing)Tier 4$() machine."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "This controller is too complex for a crafting grid. Build it on the $(item)Femtoscale Assembly Line$() - check JEI for the exact parts."
    },
    {
      "type": "patchouli:text",
      "text": "Set the three transition chances: A to B, B to C, C to A. In a ring, the feed spends time in each vat in proportion to 1/(its chance of leaving): \u03c0 \u221d (1/p, 1/q, 1/r). Each product needs its vat to hold at least three fifths of the time; thermal equilibrium needs all three nearly equal. The slowest transition sets how fast the chain mixes."
    },
